profile: tinyrustlm.startup-packet.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-09-20T16:46:20Z
canonical_memory: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-working-product-memory-2026-09-19.md
report_decision_index: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-report-intake-decision-index-2026-09-19.md

startup_steps:
  - Read workspace.uai, .uai/totem.uai, .uai/taboo.uai, canonical memory, decision index, .uai/short-term-memory.uai, .uai/operations.uai, and .uai/test-plan.uai.
  - Verify authoritative root and branch, inspect status without reverting unknown work, fetch remote, and confirm protected tree boundaries.
  - Treat reports as advisory and follow reviewed wiki/ledger routes rather than raw prose. Use workspace.uai current_companion_truth for current source state; preserve earlier checkpoint claims as historical.
  - Preserve immutable failed operations and all campaign counters.

current_truth:
  conversion_cancellation: C70 propagates caller cancellation through live input/result hashing, preserving exact identities and durable terminal evidence. All 97 Core and 228 companion tests pass; the hash loop has 100% line/branch coverage. Read conversion-hash-cancellation-review.json. Synchronous reads and uncancelled terminal reconciliation retain their limits; no real model, NuGet or deployment proof.
  candidate_selection: C69 rejects invalid explicit discovery/download limits, defaults only omission and validates the selected slice before acquisition. All 48 affected and three gate checks pass; three unchanged suites now use discoverable names. Profiles screen metadata, while the Rust CLI exposes only Qwen3/Qwen-tokenizer conversion. See candidate-selection-limits-review.json. No real model or publication evidence; converter/model gates remain.
  nuget_native_binding: C68 forces package-consumer children to their own native asset and output layout; Core conversion fixtures bind actual MSBuild output. A real missing-DLL false pass is now rejected; intact Windows packages pass. All 105 Node and 124 managed checks pass, plus audit/native smoke. See nuget-consumer-native-binding-review.json. No new Linux/ARM64 execution, key read or publication; release gates remain open.
  nuget_consumers: C67 makes the protected publisher wait for Windows x64/Linux x64/Linux ARM64 consumers of one audited package artifact. Eleven Bash entry points have executable Git modes with unchanged bytes. All 103 Node and 38 managed package checks pass plus independent YAML/Bash validation. See nuget-prepublish-consumer-review.json; hosted ARM64, source/release gates and actual publication remain open.
  terminal_prefill: C66 carries immediate context-limit completion through the worker/client with empty output and unchanged prefill KV, preserving the active model. All 113 final affected checks pass; worker/client line coverage is 81.91%/81.03%. Actual Edge boundary checks pass; the separate desktop/mobile DOM probe proves status geometry only. Read browser-terminal-prefill-review.json for historical binding correction and limitations; no real model or publication proof.
  scratch_retirement: C65 retains external ownership through locked-file, partial and terminal cleanup failures, using bounded direct unlink/rmdir. All 17 focused tests pass with 100% line coverage; shared consumers and Edge capture pass after recorded setup/binding corrections. See scratch-retirement-ownership-review.json. Quiescent writers and original ownership are required; no old-layout adoption or publication claim.
  runtime_context: C64 narrows sampling to the admitted scalar KV ceiling before prefill, retaining the last token with ContextLimit. All 76 Rust checks and Clippy pass; the refreshed local WASM reproduces twice. The 73 affected Node checks, two additional Edge scenarios and 38 related checks pass across recorded invocations. See runtime-context-limit-review.json for setup failures and coverage limits; no real model, package or public result.
  visual_capture: C63 replaces obsolete visual-lock execution with Playwright, owned profiles and current six-member input. Twenty focused checks including desktop/mobile Edge and 42 affected checks pass; line coverage 91.42%. The historical baseline still fails with 15 differences and the real CLI retains failure evidence. No product asset, real model or public result; see visual-capture-current-contract-review.json.
  memory_continuity: C62 restores the pending current-contract memory browser scenario. All 42 Node checks and one desktop Edge two-profile test pass: explicit saves only, both tiers, restore/search, replay rejection, credential nonpersistence and owned cleanup. Synthetic inference and loopback service only; no live or model claim. See browser-memory-contract-review.json.
  current_guides: C61 reconciles the four entry guides with existing MiniModel bootstrap, Advanced-only conversion, rejected diagnostic ancestry and canonical D: model storage. All 156 affected Node checks, 38 package/memory checks and twelve Edge fixture checks pass. No runtime or deployment changed; see current-product-guidance-review.json.
  companion_sockets: C60 releases owned sockets on cancellation or any failed connect, retaining success ownership in the stream. All 228 companion tests pass, including eight real IPv4/IPv6 socket cases; the socket helper has 100% line/branch coverage. Five fixture-path guesses now use current-build bindings. See companion-socket-ownership-review.json. No external TLS/DNS, model or publication proof.
  companion_hashes: C59 propagates cancellation through all five preparation and every chunk hash. All 367 affected Node checks (93.43% line coverage) and nine Edge tests pass. Real OPFS fixtures retain the prior pointer, clean candidates, release the writer and accept a subsequent install. No-signal and committed-store semantics remain; this is not real model, .NET acquisition or publication proof. See companion-hash-cancellation-review.json.
  p2p_metadata: C58 bounds all four install metadata hash waits by the existing deadline/caller signal; late rejections are observed and no later hash, store or fetch starts. All 222 affected Node checks pass (89.57% installer line coverage), with three desktop Edge acquisition tests and final desktop/mobile hash checks passing. See p2p-metadata-cancellation-review.json; synthetic fixtures do not qualify a model or seed.
  nuget_linux: C57 passes Linux x64 native build/four ABI tests, two-RID package audit, 124 managed checks and Windows/Linux packaged consumers. Windows compiled the consumer; actual Linux .NET ran it. ARM64 and clean release/publication gates remain open. Read nuget-linux-consumer-review.json and operations.uai for the blocked temporary header deletion; do not retry it or delete its parent.
  nuget_readiness: C56 blocks superseded/unknown feed observations and lookalike Trusted Publishing URLs; 86 focused and 38 managed checks pass, including full local PowerShell and WSL Bash readiness. Hosted C55 jobs never executed; operations.uai records the operator boundary. No key read or package published; C57 supplies Linux x64 proof while ARM64/release gates remain.
  nuget_windows: C55 completes actual Windows package audit and packaged-native consumer execution after correcting build path parsing, copied-source consumer setup and required P2P metadata. See nuget-consumer-build-review.json. Candidate payloads retired; no Linux or public release proof.
  nuget: Owner requires current NuGet publication. C54 records absent current package IDs, repairs false missing-package classification and removes the monitor opt-in in source. The owner supplied a local API-key file on September 20; read operations.uai nuget_publishing_credential for its location and handling. File existence is confirmed; credential validity, default-branch workflow, full native/package verification and source-authority gates remain open. No package was published.
  static_seed_browser: C53 MiniModel commit 4b815cbb877a709e8d3060c2039c13e993c334eb passes 79 checks including real Edge CORS and six exact Apache fixture bodies. Public TLS/LiteSpeed, real composition installation and qualification remain unproven.
  cache_cleanup: C52 schedules one background cleanup after successful saved-model activation or a successful check with no active installation. Sixteen passes and a 60-second cancellation signal bound new work; issued mutations retain their lock until settled. Advanced diagnostics distinguish stopping/incomplete from complete and count completed passes only. All 378 affected checks and 27 Edge tests pass; see startup-composition-cleanup-review.json. Empty cleanup creates no model root; cache/activation failures suppress it. No real-model/public gate passed.
  cache_retirement: C51 keeps external canonical staging authority until retired-directory absence is observed, reserving the active activation ID. All 369 affected checks, nine Edge tests and twelve smoke observations pass; two new Edge tests close a tab at terminal removal and resume bounded cleanup in a fresh tab. See composition-retirement-recovery-review.json. C52 adds startup scheduling; stalled mutations, power-loss durability and real-model/public gates remain separate limits.
  cache_startup: C50 gives startup cache verification one 60-second deadline. Open is read-only and OPFS root resolution is independent per operation. Timeout rejects late completion, releases the lock and shows recovery text; cache errors suppress automatic replacement pending explicit user action. Empty-cache bootstrap remains. All 336 affected checks, nineteen Edge tests and twelve direct smoke observations pass; see startup-cache-lifetime-review.json. Real-model timing, durable mutation/crash lifecycle and model/public gates remain open.
  cache_read_cancellation: C49 propagates supplied signals through metadata/member acquisition, metadata streams/hashes, enumeration and candidate validation. Cancellation remains distinct from corrupt data; pointer commit/readback still reconciles. See composition-read-cancellation-review.json. C50 supplies startup's signal; general signal-free calls, durable mutations and terminal orphan cleanup retain their separate lifetime limits.
  cache_readers: C48 gives each composition shared read leases and exclusive write/retirement locks. The app pins all six cached files through worker activation; companion validation requires withRead. Scope cleanup and cancellation release readers; actual Edge tabs prove waiting and release on closure. See composition-read-lease-review.json. Remaining crash/metadata lifetime and real model/public gates stay open.
  cache_ownership: C47 rejects unknown staging/installed content, bounds ownership inventories and removes only recognized direct files. Recovery keeps invalid pointer authority until content deletion succeeds; failed candidates keep markers on failed cleanup. All 143 affected checks, three Edge storage tests and twelve direct smoke observations pass; see composition-cleanup-ownership-review.json. Reader/crash lifecycle and real model/public gates remain open.
  cache_cancellation: C46 fixes a stalled source-cleanup wait that ignored later cancellation. All 118 affected checks, two Edge OPFS/cache tests and twelve direct smoke observations pass. Previous installation and lock availability are preserved; supplied signals are required. See composition-cleanup-cancellation-review.json. Whole-cache review and real model/public gates remain open.
  release_smoke: C45 v8 retains raw abort events and separately attributes only exact HTTP 200 probe bodies after independent byte verification. Minimal-page trials reproduced the distinction; bounded terminal-event waits replace a stalled Playwright response wait. All 34 smoke and 42 unchanged runtime checks plus the normal CLI pass. See completed-runtime-probe-review.json; no real model or public result.
  runtime_lifetime: C43 defers runtime download until a model operation, adds one 60-second deadline and cancellation through the shared admission/runtime helper, and reserves activation ownership before waiting. 262 focused, 26 artifact/publication and 14 Edge chooser checks pass. See browser-runtime-lifetime-review.json; model/public gates remain open.
  runtime_bytes: C42 bounds decoded runtime downloads before allocation/copy and moves build checks into owned canonical artifacts. All 48 checks pass; two offline builds exactly reproduce the tracked WASM after binding virtual profile mapping. See browser-runtime-streaming-review.json. No promotion, real model or public result.
  admission_lifetime: C41 gives browser qualification/admission checks one 30-second deadline plus explicit cancellation. 218 JavaScript and eight installed-Edge fixture checks pass; see admission-lifetime-review.json. Real-model/public gates remain open.
  companion: Production source acquisition, exclusive operation ownership, contained conversion, terminal reconciliation, six-member transfer, and listener wiring are implemented; Available is not model qualification.
  blocker: No authorized real-source acquisition receipt through this coordinator or qualified real model is established by the implementation and fixture evidence.
  browser: Current worktree product UI loads the capability client and composition installer; source wiring is not real-model browser or deployment proof.
  next_gate: Use the reviewed five-experiment plan; establish eligible source usefulness, fresh current v3 material registration and real native/WASM/browser evidence. Discover hosting capabilities independently; no replay of closed operations.
  candidate_gate: C39 retires the incompatible Qwen-only v1 producer; supported-profile discovery is the sole current v2 owner, with corrected access flags. Forty-five affected checks pass, retaining C35-C38 exclusions, bounds and owned receipts. Independent admission and real model gates remain; no-match is not admission.
  task_screen: C40 retires three superseded evaluators and old generator; useful checks now exercise v4/generator v2. All 17 frozen records remain unchanged and closed; 20 affected checks pass. See current-task-screen-review.json; no real model or new execution authority.
  current_state_details: workspace.uai
  companion_source: dotnet/src/TinyRustLM.Companion/CompanionProductionOperationRuntime.cs
  browser_source: tinyrustlm/app/index.html
